# Mastodon follow Grammy nomination and ‘GTA 6’ appearance with first UK and European tour in eight years

> 🎵 *Curated Music Story from NME Music Official Publications*

### 📖 The Full Story

Music News Mastodon follow Grammy nomination and ‘GTA 6’ appearance with first UK and European tour in eight years Tickets are on sale now By Tom Skinner | 27th November 2026 Mastodon, 2026. CREDIT: William Lacalmontie/PRESS

Mastodon have announced their first UK and European tour in eight years for 2027. Find all the details below.

The US metal band will hit the road in March, kicking off the trek with a show at L’Olympia in Paris. From there, they’ll head to Bilbao, Lisbon, Barcelona, Luxembourg, Cologne and other European cities throughout the month.

### 🎤 Key Highlights & Community Reactions

Troy Sanders and co. are then scheduled to touch down in the UK on March 30, when they’ll take to the stage at London’s O2 Academy Brixton. Further gigs on these shores are set to take place in Manchester, Glasgow and Birmingham in early April.

Mastodon will return to Europe shortly afterwards for more concerts in cities such as Brussels, Munich, Budapest, Berlin, Helsinki, Stockholm, Oslo, Copenhagen and Hamburg.

Green Lung are opening for Mastodon in the UK, with Swedish doom metal trio Monolord supporting at all dates.

Tickets for the upcoming 28-stop ‘Poisonous Weapons’ tour went on general sale this morning (Friday November 27) – you can buy yours here .

